; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Dragon Pinwheel
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, dragon curve, paper folding, color
; SUMMARY:  Draws four dragon curves from the center that fit together like a pinwheel.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Fold a strip of paper in half again and again, open it out so
;   every fold is a right angle, and you get the dragon curve. This
;   program draws four dragons starting at the middle of the screen,
;   each turned a quarter turn from the last. They never cross, they
;   just fit snugly into each other's gaps.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the level and size at the bottom. Keep
;   size times 2 to the power (level / 2) about the same.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a single procedure with a :sign input instead of two procedures
;   * how folding doubles the number of segments at every level
;   * running the same drawing at four headings with FOR
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw only two dragons, at heading 0 and 180.
;   * Change the 90 degree turn to 80. The dragon starts to curl.
;   * Use level 14 with size 2. Be patient.
; ============================================================

; DRAGON draws one dragon curve. :sign is 1 or -1 and says which way
; the middle fold turns. The second half is always folded the
; opposite way, which is why the second call passes -1.
to dragon :size :level :sign
  if :level = 0 [forward :size stop]
  dragon :size :level - 1 1
  right 90 * :sign
  dragon :size :level - 1 -1
end

; WING draws one dragon from the center pointing toward :heading.
to wing :heading :color
  penup home pendown
  setheading :heading
  setpencolor :color
  dragon 6 11 1
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [25 25 35]
setpensize 2
make "colors [[240 80 70] [250 190 60] [80 200 120] [80 150 250]]
for [k 1 4] [wing 90 * :k item :k :colors]
